{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"getting-started.png","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By the end of this guide you will have a game with two rooms, one object, one rule, and a test that plays it. It assumes you can write basic Swift; it assumes nothing about interactive fiction."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prefer to start from something that already runs? "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bin\/new-game Zwank ~\/dev\/Zwank"},{"type":"text","text":" writes a complete starter package named for your game — then skim this guide for the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}]},{"type":"text","text":" behind each piece."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Add-Gnusto-to-your-package","type":"heading","text":"Add Gnusto to your package"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These articles describe the engine on ","type":"text"},{"code":"main","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so pin the newest release: ","type":"text"},{"code":"bin\/new-game","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads it from the repository’s tags, and if a name an article uses fails to compile in your package, the pin is behind the article. Building against a checkout instead (","type":"text"},{"code":"bin\/new-game --dep-path","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") cannot fall behind.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Gnusto as a dependency, list it in your executable target, and give the test target the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoTestSupport"},{"type":"text","text":" product (it links the toolchain’s Testing library, so it belongs in test targets only):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ swift-tools-version: 6.2","import PackageDescription","","let package = Package(","    name: \"MyGame\",","    platforms: [.macOS(.v15)],","    dependencies: [","        .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/Gnusto\", from: \"0.6.0\")","    ],","    targets: [","        .executableTarget(","            name: \"MyGame\",","            dependencies: [","                .product(name: \"Gnusto\", package: \"Gnusto\")","            ]","        ),","        .testTarget(","            name: \"MyGameTests\",","            dependencies: [","                \"MyGame\",","                .product(name: \"GnustoTestSupport\", package: \"Gnusto\"),","            ]","        ),","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gnusto needs a Swift 6.2 toolchain and the Swift 6 language mode. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macOS(.v15)"},{"type":"text","text":" floor above is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Synchronization.Mutex"},{"type":"text","text":"; Linux is tested in CI and needs no platform line. iOS is supported too, at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".iOS(.v18)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the same reason. Add that line if your game is an app rather than a terminal program, and give it an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" of its own — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Declare a game","anchor":"Declare-a-game","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A game is a single type conforming to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":". Start with just a title and an intro:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Gnusto","","struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":" requires an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":", but Swift synthesizes it for free as long as every stored property has a default value — which they always will here, since rooms, items, and state are declared with initializers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add a room","anchor":"Add-a-room","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location"},{"type":"text","text":" as a stored property. The property name ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hall"},{"type":"text","text":") becomes the room’s internal identity; the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" trait is what the player sees."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","","    let hall = Location {","        name(\"Entrance Hall\")","        description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","    }","","    var map: WorldMap {","        player.starts(in: hall)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block is where geography and starting positions live. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player.starts(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" places the player; without it, the game has nowhere to begin."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Run it","anchor":"Run-it","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two lines turn a game value into a running session:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld"},{"type":"text","text":" validates the game and builds its initial state up front — a mistake like an exit to an undeclared room is caught here, as a thrown "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError"},{"type":"text","text":", not at runtime. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL"},{"type":"text","text":" runs the prompt\/parse\/perform\/print loop, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" reads from and writes to the terminal."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wrap it in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"catch"},{"type":"text","text":" in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Gnusto","","do {","    let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","    await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()","} catch {","    print(\"Couldn't start the game: \\(error)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift run"},{"type":"text","text":", and you can already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"look"},{"type":"text","text":" around and try to move."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add a second room and connect them","anchor":"Add-a-second-room-and-connect-them","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are declared on locations in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block. Each directional method ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", …) is an ordinary property reference, so a typo or a renamed room is a compile error, not a broken game."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let hall = Location {","    name(\"Entrance Hall\")","    description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","}","","let library = Location {","    name(\"Dusty Library\")","    description(\"Shelves sag under mildewed books. The hall lies south.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-directional by design — declare both "},{"code":"hall.north(library)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"library.south(hall)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if you want the player to be able to walk back."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Add a thing","anchor":"Add-a-thing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" the same way, then place it in the "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    adjectives(\"brass\", \"old\")","    description(\"An old brass lantern, its glass sooty but intact.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","    lantern.starts(in: library)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the player can walk "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"north"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"examine lantern"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take lantern"},{"text":", and see it in their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inventory"},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" let them type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take brass lantern"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take old lantern"},{"type":"text","text":"; a phrase has to end on a noun, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take brass"},{"type":"text","text":" on its own is not one of them. The last word of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (“lantern”) is the noun the parser keys on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything you declare is split into words the same way the parser splits what the player types — lowercased, a trailing possessive dropped, every other punctuation mark a separator. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(\"Mrs. Vane\")"},{"type":"text","text":" prints its period and answers to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mrs vane"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjectives(\"master's\")"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same declaration as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjectives(\"master\")"},{"text":". Write the second: a declaration should read the way the parser stores it.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"React-with-a-rule","text":"React with a rule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So far every verb uses its built-in behavior. To add your own logic, write a rule in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" block. Rules are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":" hooks attached to a location, an item, or the whole world."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var rules: Rules {","    lantern.after(.take) {","        say(\"It's heavier than it looks.\")","    }","","    library.before(.go) {","        guard command.direction != .south else { return }","        try refuse(\"There's no exit that way — only back south to the hall.\")","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first rule runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the player successfully takes the lantern and adds a line of flavor with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The second runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"text":" movement in the library and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":"s any direction but south. Inside a rule body, bare identifiers like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lantern"},{"type":"text","text":" refer to the live turn — reading and writing them touches the current game state."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To learn what rules can do — the phases, the ordering, and the difference between "},{"code":"refuse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"reply","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"say"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"end","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — read ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Test-it","text":"Test it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A play session is just typed input and printed output, so the natural test plays a scripted session and asserts on the transcript:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","struct MyGameTests {","    @Test func theLanternIsWhereTheBreezeSaysItIs() async throws {","        let transcript = try await play(MyGame(), [\"north\", \"take lantern\"])","        expectInOrder(transcript, [\"Dusty Library\", \"Taken.\"])","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"play","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" boots the game and feeds it each command; "},{"code":"expectInOrder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" asserts the beats appear in order and shows the full transcript when one doesn’t. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for turn slicing and pinning the random stream."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-fuller-example","text":"A fuller example","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gnusto ships with "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cloak of Darkness","type":"text"}]},{"text":", Roger Firth’s classic one-room demonstration game, as its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CloakOfDarkness"},{"type":"text","text":" target. It exercises nearly every feature in a page of code — dark rooms, a wearable cloak, scored actions, a losing state, and per-turn rules — and is worth reading start to finish once the basics click."}]},{"text":"Next steps","anchor":"Next-steps","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bin\/new-game"},{"text":" in the repo — writes the complete starter package this guide builds up to","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — how declarations, identity, and live references fit together","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","type":"reference"},{"text":" — exactly what happens each turn","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — the full vocabulary of game logic","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — teach the parser new words with "},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — transcript tests with GnustoTestSupport","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — carry your own data on entities and in globals"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"Getting Started with Gnusto","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AnatomyOfAGame":{"role":"article","title":"Anatomy of a Game","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/south(_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"south"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","text":"Location"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV","text":"MapEntry"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)","title":"south(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/south(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An exit leading south to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"role":"article","title":"The Turn Pipeline","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline","abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","title":"Gnusto","role":"collection"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/IOHandler":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IOHandler"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IOHandler"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/iohandler","title":"IOHandler","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the game’s text goes and player input comes from. Synchronous by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"design: a blocking console read is fine for a CLI; an async variant can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be added later without breaking this protocol’s clients."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Location","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Location","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A place in the world."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/say(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/say(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"say"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"say(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Prints a message as part of the turn’s output.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameWorld":{"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameworld","title":"GameWorld","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The game world: owns all state, serializes all mutation, and runs the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turn pipeline. The single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" in a game sits between the REPL and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this actor."}]},"getting-started.png":{"identifier":"getting-started.png","alt":"A lantern lights an open stone doorway and the stairs beyond.","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/Gnusto\/getting-started@2x.png","traits":["2x","light"]}],"type":"image"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/refuse(_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refuse","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","text":"Never","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"refuse(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/refuse(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Blocks the current action with a complaint. The default action and any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"remaining "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":" rules are skipped; world time still passes."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/north(_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"north"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","text":"Location","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV","text":"MapEntry","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)","title":"no